			`<p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">${'The difference runs through the divine name as well. The New World Translation prints “Jehovah” thousands of times, including in the New Testament, where no Greek manuscript has the divine name. Father’s Heart Bible™ renders YHWH by the Person it refers to, and where the New Testament identifies that Person as Jesus, it names Jesus.'}</p>` +
